On 2008-04-29, Mikael Lind <mikkelin@gmail.com> wrote:
>   - Automatically redistribute skill points so that frequently and
>     recently used skills tend to have Expert level, while infrequently
>     and not recently used skills tend to have Basic level.

This doesn't lend itself well to Nethack's play, especially from the
perspective of spell skills -- since a spellcaster may indeed not need
to use spells from a certain school.  As far as weapon skills go, it is
fairly rare for characters to swap out weapons, so the player won't see
any significant change from present.

The other downside is that this encourages artificial play; ie. spend a
certain number of turns throwing daggers so your dagger skill doesn't go
down, then switch back to Frost Brand, then switch back to daggers...
etc.  This really isn't fun for the player, especially if the most
effective means of dealing with the problem is just to wade through the
critters.

("victory dancing" is already a problem in Nethack, so while this also
increases the player's tendency to do same, it isn't anything new.)

